<h1>Import / Export</h1>

<section class="two">
  <form class="card" method="post" action="/import" enctype="multipart/form-data">
    <h2>Import</h2>
    <p>Upload any of these. The format is detected automatically, and re-importing is safe because books are matched by ISBN, or by title and author.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Goodreads</strong>: My Books → Import and export → Export Library (CSV)</li>
      <li><strong>StoryGraph</strong>: Manage Account → Export StoryGraph Library (CSV)</li>
      <li><strong>Booklog JSON</strong>: this app's own export, or any schema.org Review/Book JSON</li>
    </ul>
    <input type="file" name="file" accept=".csv,.json,text/csv,application/json" required>
    <button>Import</button>
  </form>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Export</h2>
    <p><a class="button" href="/export.json">Booklog JSON</a> Lossless. Includes reads, loans, quarter-star ratings and community ratings. Valid <a href="https://schema.org/Book">schema.org</a> JSON-LD. <a href="/schema/booklog.schema.json">Schema</a>.</p>
    <p><a class="button" href="/export.csv">Goodreads CSV</a> The format everything else imports, including StoryGraph, BookWyrm and Goodreads. Ratings are rounded to whole stars, and only your last read date is kept.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Metadata &amp; community ratings</h2>
  <% if @enrich[:running] %>
    <p>Fetching… <%= @enrich[:done] %> / <%= @enrich[:total] %>. <a href="/import">Refresh</a></p>
  <% elsif @pending > 0 %>
    <p><%= @pending %> books haven't been looked up on Open Library yet. That lookup fills in covers, missing details and community ratings.</p>
    <form method="post" action="/enrich"><button>Fetch in background</button></form>
  <% else %>
    <p class="muted">Everything has been looked up. Run <code>bin/enrich --all</code> to refresh community ratings.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>
